{"id":"mahabharata-12-076","work":"mahabharata","part":12,"partName":"शान्तिपर्व","partNameEn":"Shanti Parva","unit":76,"title":"षट्सप्ततितमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 76 · How a king grows","summary":{"en":"Yudhishthira asks what conduct makes a king grow in power and win heaven, and Bhishma says he must be gentle and firm and protect all. He tells that those who live on the king's support look to him as to a cloud or a great tree, and should be fostered.","kn":"ಯಾವ ನಡತೆ ರಾಜನನ್ನು ಬಲಶಾಲಿ ಮಾಡಿ ಸ್ವರ್ಗ ತರುತ್ತದೆಂದು ಯುಧಿಷ್ಠಿರ ಕೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಮೃದು, ದೃಢನಾಗಿ ಎಲ್ಲರನ್ನೂ ರಕ್ಷಿಸಬೇಕೆಂದು ಭೀಷ್ಮ ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ. ರಾಜನ ಆಶ್ರಯದಲ್ಲಿ ಬದುಕುವವರು ಮೇಘ, ಮಹಾವೃಕ್ಷದಂತೆ ಅವನನ್ನು ನೋಡುತ್ತಾರೆ, ಅವರನ್ನು ಪೋಷಿಸಬೇಕು.","hi":"युधिष्ठिर पूछते हैं कि किस आचरण से राजा बल बढ़ाकर स्वर्ग पाता है, और भीष्म कहते हैं कि वह कोमल और दृढ़ रहकर सबकी रक्षा करे। राजा के सहारे जीने वाले उसे मेघ या महावृक्ष की तरह देखते हैं और उनका पोषण होना चाहिए।","te":"ఏ ప్రవర్తన రాజును బలవంతుని చేసి స్వర్గం ఇస్తుందని యుధిష్ఠిరుడు అడుగుతాడు; మృదువుగా, దృఢంగా ఉండి అందరినీ రక్షించాలని భీష్ముడు చెబుతాడు. రాజు ఆశ్రయంతో బతికేవారు అతన్ని మేఘంలా, మహావృక్షంలా చూస్తారు, వారిని పోషించాలి.","ta":"எந்த நடத்தை மன்னனை வலிமையாக்கிச் சொர்க்கம் தரும் என்று யுதிஷ்டிரர் கேட்க, மென்மையும் உறுதியுமாக எல்லோரையும் காக்க வேண்டும் என்று பீஷ்மர் கூறுகிறார். மன்னனை நம்பி வாழ்வோர் அவனை மேகம் போல், பெருமரம் போல் பார்க்கின்றனர், அவர்களைப் பேண வேண்டும்.","ml":"ഏതു നടപ്പാണ് രാജാവിന്റെ ശക്തി വളർത്തി സ്വർഗ്ഗം നേടിക്കൊടുക്കുന്നതെന്ന് യുധിഷ്ഠിരൻ ചോദിക്കുന്നു; മൃദുവും ദൃഢവുമായിരിക്കണമെന്നും എല്ലാവരെയും സംരക്ഷിക്കണമെന്നും ഭീഷ്മർ പറയുന്നു. രാജാവിന്റെ പിന്തുണയിൽ ജീവിക്കുന്നവർ അദ്ദേഹത്തെ മേഘത്തെയോ വലിയ മരത്തെയോ പോലെ നോക്കുന്നുവെന്നും, അവരെ പോഷിപ്പിക്കണമെന്നും അദ്ദേഹം പറയുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 12.76; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Wed Jun 16 2021","sections":[{"title":"राजधर्मपर्व","titleEn":"Rajadharma Parva (Duties of kings)","verses":[{"text":"युधिष्ठिर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"यया वृत्त्या महीपालो विवर्धयति मानवान् ।\nपुण्यांश्च लोकाञ्जयति तन्मे ब्रूहि पितामह ॥","meaning":{"en":"Grandfather, tell me by what conduct a king makes his people prosper and wins the worlds of merit."}},{"text":"भीष्म उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma said:"}},{"n":2,"text":"दानशीलो भवेद्राजा यज्ञशीलश्च भारत ।\nउपवासतपःशीलः प्रजानां पालने रतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"A king should be given to giving and sacrifice, to fasting and austerity, and delight in protecting the people."}},{"n":3,"text":"सर्वाश्चैव प्रजा नित्यं राजा धर्मेण पालयेत् ।\nउत्थानेनाप्रमादेन पूजयेच्चैव धार्मिकान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"A king should always guard all the people righteously, with effort and without carelessness, and honour the righteous."}},{"n":4,"text":"राज्ञा हि पूजितो धर्मस्ततः सर्वत्र पूज्यते ।\nयद्यदाचरते राजा तत्प्रजानां हि रोचते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Righteousness honoured by the king is then honoured everywhere; whatever the king does, the people like."}},{"n":5,"text":"नित्यमुद्यतदण्डश्च भवेन्मृत्युरिवारिषु ।\nनिहन्यात्सर्वतो दस्यून्न कामात्कस्यचित्क्षमेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He should always keep the rod raised, like death for his enemies; he should kill robbers everywhere and not forgive anyone out of favour."}},{"n":6,"text":"यं हि धर्मं चरन्तीह प्रजा राज्ञा सुरक्षिताः ।\nचतुर्थं तस्य धर्मस्य राजा भारत विन्दति ॥","meaning":{"en":"The righteousness the people practise here, well protected by the king, a fourth part of it the king gets, Bharata."}},{"n":7,"text":"यदधीते यद्यजते यद्ददाति यदर्चति ।\nराजा चतुर्थभाक्तस्य प्रजा धर्मेण पालयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Whatever they study, sacrifice, give and worship, the king, guarding the people righteously, takes a fourth part of it."}},{"n":8,"text":"यद्राष्ट्रेऽकुशलं किंचिद्राज्ञोऽरक्षयतः प्रजाः ।\nचतुर्थं तस्य पापस्य राजा भारत विन्दति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Whatever harm happens in the kingdom when the king fails to protect the people, the king takes a fourth part of that sin, Bharata."}},{"n":9,"text":"अप्याहुः सर्वमेवेति भूयोऽर्धमिति निश्चयः ।\nकर्मणः पृथिवीपाल नृशंसोऽनृतवागपि ।\nतादृशात्किल्बिषाद्राजा शृणु येन प्रमुच्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Some say he gets all of it, and the settled view is more than half; when a king is cruel or false in speech, protector of the earth, hear by what means he is freed from such guilt."}},{"n":10,"text":"प्रत्याहर्तुमशक्यं स्याद्धनं चोरैर्हृतं यदि ।\nस्वकोशात्तत्प्रदेयं स्यादशक्तेनोपजीवता ॥","meaning":{"en":"If wealth carried off by thieves cannot be recovered, it must be paid from his own treasury, if he lives by it and is unable to recover it."}},{"n":11,"text":"सर्ववर्णैः सदा रक्ष्यं ब्रह्मस्वं ब्राह्मणास्तथा ।\nन स्थेयं विषये तेषु योऽपकुर्याद्द्विजातिषु ॥","meaning":{"en":"Brahmana property and Brahmanas must always be protected by all classes; one must not stay in a land where someone wrongs the twice-born."}},{"n":12,"text":"ब्रह्मस्वे रक्ष्यमाणे हि सर्वं भवति रक्षितम् ।\nतेषां प्रसादे निर्वृत्ते कृतकृत्यो भवेन्नृपः ॥","meaning":{"en":"If Brahmana property is protected, everything is protected; when they are pleased, the king has done what was to be done."}},{"n":13,"text":"पर्जन्यमिव भूतानि महाद्रुममिव द्विजाः ।\nनरास्तमुपजीवन्ति नृपं सर्वार्थसाधकम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As beings depend on the rain cloud and birds on a great tree, men depend on the king, who accomplishes all aims."}},{"n":14,"text":"न हि कामात्मना राज्ञा सततं शठबुद्धिना ।\nनृशंसेनातिलुब्धेन शक्याः पालयितुं प्रजाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"A king who is ruled by desire, always crooked in mind, cruel and very greedy cannot protect the people."}},{"text":"युधिष्ठिर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira said:"}},{"n":15,"text":"नाहं राज्यसुखान्वेषी राज्यमिच्छाम्यपि क्षणम् ।\nधर्मार्थं रोचये राज्यं धर्मश्चात्र न विद्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"I do not seek the pleasures of kingship and do not want a kingdom even for a moment. I like a kingdom for the sake of righteousness, and there is no righteousness in it."}},{"n":16,"text":"तदलं मम राज्येन यत्र धर्मो न विद्यते ।\nवनमेव गमिष्यामि तस्माद्धर्मचिकीर्षया ॥","meaning":{"en":"So enough of a kingdom where there is no righteousness; from the wish to do right I shall go to the forest."}},{"n":17,"text":"तत्र मेध्येष्वरण्येषु न्यस्तदण्डो जितेन्द्रियः ।\nधर्ममाराधयिष्यामि मुनिर्मूलफलाशनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"There, in the pure forests, laying down the rod and controlling my senses, I shall worship righteousness as a sage living on roots and fruits."}},{"text":"भीष्म उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma said:"}},{"n":18,"text":"वेदाहं तव या बुद्धिरानृशंस्यगुणैव सा ।\nन च शुद्धानृशंस्येन शक्यं महदुपासितुम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"I know your mind: it is made up of the quality of mercy. But great ends cannot be gained by pure mercy alone."}},{"n":19,"text":"अपि तु त्वा मृदुं दान्तमत्यार्यमतिधार्मिकम् ।\nक्लीबं धर्मघृणायुक्तं न लोको बहु मन्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"The world does not esteem a man who is gentle, restrained, over-noble, over-righteous and weak, and filled with pity for righteousness."}},{"n":20,"text":"राजधर्मानवेक्षस्व पितृपैतामहोचितान् ।\nनैतद्राज्ञामथो वृत्तं यथा त्वं स्थातुमिच्छसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Look to the royal duties suited to your father and grandfather; what you wish to follow is not the way of kings."}},{"n":21,"text":"न हि वैक्लव्यसंसृष्टमानृशंस्यमिहास्थितः ।\nप्रजापालनसंभूतं प्राप्ता धर्मफलं ह्यसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"You have not obtained here the fruit of righteousness by mercy mixed with weakness; you have it from protecting the people."}},{"n":22,"text":"न ह्येतामाशिषं पाण्डुर्न च कुन्त्यन्वयाचत ।\nन चैतां प्राज्ञतां तात यया चरसि मेधया ॥","meaning":{"en":"Neither Pandu nor Kunti ever asked for this blessing for you, nor for this kind of wisdom, my child, by which you now behave."}},{"n":23,"text":"शौर्यं बलं च सत्त्वं च पिता तव सदाब्रवीत् ।\nमाहात्म्यं बलमौदार्यं तव कुन्त्यन्वयाचत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Your father always spoke of valour, strength and spirit; and Kunti asked for greatness, strength and generosity for you."}},{"n":24,"text":"नित्यं स्वाहा स्वधा नित्यमुभे मानुषदैवते ।\nपुत्रेष्वाशासते नित्यं पितरो दैवतानि च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Always svaha and svadha, both the human and the divine offerings, the ancestors and the gods always hope for from their sons."}},{"n":25,"text":"दानमध्ययनं यज्ञः प्रजानां परिपालनम् ।\nधर्ममेतमधर्मं वा जन्मनैवाभ्यजायिथाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Giving, study, sacrifice and protecting the people: this duty, or its opposite, you were born to by birth itself."}},{"n":26,"text":"काले धुरि नियुक्तानां वहतां भार आहिते ।\nसीदतामपि कौन्तेय न कीर्तिरवसीदति ॥","meaning":{"en":"For those set in due time to the yoke who carry the load laid on them, even if they sink down, their fame does not sink, son of Kunti."}},{"n":27,"text":"समन्ततो विनियतो वहत्यस्खलितो हि यः ।\nनिर्दोषकर्मवचनात्सिद्धिः कर्मण एव सा ॥","meaning":{"en":"One who is held back on all sides and still carries on without stumbling, by the blameless action and word, his success is just that of action."}},{"n":28,"text":"नैकान्तविनिपातेन विचचारेह कश्चन ।\nधर्मी गृही वा राजा वा ब्रह्मचार्यथ वा पुनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"No one here, whether the righteous, a householder, a king or a celibate student, has moved through the world by utter ruin."}},{"n":29,"text":"अल्पं तु साधुभूयिष्ठं यत्कर्मोदारमेव तत् ।\nकृतमेवाकृताच्छ्रेयो न पापीयोऽस्त्यकर्मणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Even a small act, if mostly good, is a noble act; an act done is better than one not done, and nothing is worse than inaction."}},{"n":30,"text":"यदा कुलीनो धर्मज्ञः प्राप्नोत्यैश्वर्यमुत्तमम् ।\nयोगक्षेमस्तदा राजन्कुशलायैव कल्पते ॥","meaning":{"en":"When a high-born man who knows righteousness gains supreme sovereignty, then, king, the gaining and keeping of goods leads only to welfare."}},{"n":31,"text":"दानेनान्यं बलेनान्यमन्यं सूनृतया गिरा ।\nसर्वतः परिगृह्णीयाद्राज्यं प्राप्येह धार्मिकः ॥","meaning":{"en":"A righteous man who has gained a kingdom here should win over one by giving, another by force and another by kind words, from every side."}},{"n":32,"text":"यं हि वैद्याः कुले जाता अवृत्तिभयपीडिताः ।\nप्राप्य तृप्ताः प्रतिष्ठन्ति धर्मः कोऽभ्यधिकस्ततः ॥","meaning":{"en":"What higher righteousness is there than this, that learned men born in good families, afflicted by fear of want, find satisfaction and a firm footing through him?"}},{"text":"युधिष्ठिर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira said:"}},{"n":33,"text":"किं न्वतः परमं स्वर्ग्यं का न्वतः प्रीतिरुत्तमा ।\nकिं न्वतः परमैश्वर्यं ब्रूहि मे यदि मन्यसे ॥","meaning":{"en":"What is better than this for heaven, what better joy, what greater lordship? Tell me, if you think fit."}},{"text":"भीष्म उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma said:"}},{"n":34,"text":"यस्मिन्प्रतिष्ठिताः सम्यक्क्षेमं विन्दन्ति तत्क्षणम् ।\nस स्वर्गजित्तमोऽस्माकं सत्यमेतद्ब्रवीमि ते ॥","meaning":{"en":"The one in whom, when well established, people find well-being at once is the best winner of heaven among us; this I tell you truly."}},{"n":35,"text":"त्वमेव प्रीतिमांस्तस्मात्कुरूणां कुरुसत्तम ।\nभव राजा जय स्वर्गं सतो रक्षासतो जहि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Therefore you alone are the one who is happy, best of the Kurus. Be king, win heaven, protect the good and kill the wicked."}},{"n":36,"text":"अनु त्वा तात जीवन्तु सुहृदः साधुभिः सह ।\nपर्जन्यमिव भूतानि स्वादुद्रुममिवाण्डजाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"May your friends live on you together with the good, my son, as beings live on the rain cloud and birds on a tree with sweet fruit."}},{"n":37,"text":"धृष्टं शूरं प्रहर्तारमनृशंसं जितेन्द्रियम् ।\nवत्सलं संविभक्तारमनु जीवन्तु त्वां जनाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"May people live on you, bold, brave, a striker, gentle, self-controlled, affectionate and a fair sharer."}}]}]}